                            <tr><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>144</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>3</td><td>9</td><td>13</td><td>169</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>4</td><td>16</td><td>14</td><td>196</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>5</td><td>25</td><td>15</td><td>225</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>6</td><td>36</td><td>16</td><td>256</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>7</td><td>49</td><td>17</td><td>289</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>8</td><td>64</td><td>18</td><td>324</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>9</td><td>81</td><td>19</td><td>361</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>10</td><td>100</td><td>20</td><td>400</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>If you can recognize these on sight, spotting perfect squares (and simplifying square roots) becomes second nature.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section: FAQs -->
        <section class="article-section article-section--alt" id="section-faqs">
            <div class="article-container">
                <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg></span> FAQs</div>
                <h2 class="article-h2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <div class="faq-list">
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">How do I use the Racine Carree Calculator?</h3>
                        <p>Type any number into the box above, click Calculate, and the tool instantly shows you the square root — including a simplified form when one exists and support for negative numbers.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">Can I calculate square roots manually?</h3>
                        <p>Yes. For perfect squares, prime factorization works well. For everything else, the long division method or the estimation trick (finding which two perfect squares your number sits between) will get you there — just more slowly than a calculator.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">What does "racine carrée" mean?</h3>
                        <p>It's French for "square root." A racine carrée calculator and a square root calculator do exactly the same job — the name just reflects that a lot of English-speaking users search using the French phrase.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">Why is the keyword "racine carrée" in French?</h3>
                        <p>It's a quirk of how people search. Even though this site and its explanations are written in English, "racine carrée" shows up as a common search term among US, UK, and Canadian users — likely from French class, Canadian bilingual schooling, or simply how the term was first learned.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">Can I calculate square roots of decimals or large numbers?</h3>
                        <p>Yes. The calculator handles decimals, whole numbers, and large values with high precision, so you don't need to worry about the size or format of what you're entering.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">Can the calculator handle negative numbers?</h3>
                        <p>Yes. When you enter a negative number, the calculator returns the result using the imaginary unit "i," as explained in the section above.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3 class="article-h3">Is this calculator free to use?</h3>
                        <p>Yes, completely — no sign-up, no downloads, no limits on how many times you use it.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

